  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 221 AM EDT Thursday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1: \n\nWidespread precipitation continues to push through the region this \nhour, although rainfall amounts are not nearly impressive as they \nwere earlier in the night when KMSS measured over 3 inches of \nrainfall within a fairly short window. Showers will trend more \nscattered as the day progresses, with the best chances for \nadditional rainfall across eastern Vermont and the northern Green \nMountains although amounts will generally be light. Gusty southerly \nwinds continue across the region this hour, particularly on Lake \nChamplain, but will diminish towards daybreak and become more \nnorthwesterly by this afternoon. Additional chances for diurnally \ndriven showers will continue through the rest of the week, with the \ngreatest chances across the high terrain while the broader valleys \nremain on the drier side. High pressure looks to build in\ntowards Sunday, bringing some drier weather. Temperatures will \nbe on the cooler side as we remain under the influence of an \nupper low, with high temperatures generally in the upper 60s to \nmid 70s by this weekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Deep layer ridging will make a brief appearance on \nMonday bringing sunshine, light winds and seasonal temperatures to \nthe North Country and northern New York. This period of dry weather \nwill be short-lived as a shortwave trough in the northwesterly flow \naloft flattens the longwave ridge and drives a cold front through \nthe region Monday night into Tuesday morning. This should spark a \nfew showers but no thunderstorms or impactful weather are expected \nwith this system as we will seriously lack deep moisture. \nThereafter, a series of low amplitude shortwaves are expected to \nmove across the region through the second half of the work week. \nPeriod of light showers seem plausible through much of the week with \nample period of dry weather between rounds of showers. However, if \nyou are looking for an extended period of dry weather, next week \ndoes not look favorable for that at this time.",
